  "title": "Images gained references",
  "summary": "September brought more ways to generate and edit images, a clearer path to API access through Enter, and a wider range of community-built tools.\n\nNanobanana and Seedream joined the image API, and the editor gained support for up to four reference images on supported models. Queue changes gave Flower and Nectar users more room for image requests.\n\nEnter added GitHub sign-in, API key management, a Pollen balance view, and routes for free and paid generation. Later changes simplified the account page and made balance checks and request tracking more precise.\n\nFamiliar OpenAI model IDs were reassigned as GPT-5 Mini and Nano arrived; DeepSeek V3.1 and search-grounded Gemini were also added. Token caps and routing changes made model behavior more predictable.\n\nThe community directory grew with image generators, chat apps, a collaborative comics tool, developer utilities, and projects in Japanese, Portuguese, Persian, and Turkish.",
